From 7b545e64c28b102ca1e0f1c3275e61fb031c3833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:59:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Store the conversation and replay the last turns
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nothing about a chat survived the request. The answer went back to the browser,
the browser held it in component state, and a refresh erased it. Two things
followed from that: a follow-up question reached the model with no idea what
had just been discussed, so "a čo tie lieky?" had no referent for "tie"; and
there was no record of what the app had told the patient, which a health
product has to be able to produce.

chat_messages stores both sides of every turn with a timestamp. The last six
are replayed ahead of the question — questions and answers only, since the
health context is rebuilt from the database each time and would otherwise be
paid for once per remembered turn, and a replayed answer is trimmed because a
follow-up needs the subject, not the whole report.

GET /api/chat/history returns the conversation with timestamps and the full
text of every answer. The deployed frontend needs no change for the memory to
work; this endpoint is how the history can be read until the UI shows it.

Loading and saving are both best-effort: the session is acquired inside the
try, so an unreachable database costs the memory rather than the answer.

